WEBVTT

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:03.310
<b>Culture Festival</b>

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:05.900
<b>Frankfurters</b>

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.730
<b>Strawberry
 Banana
Crêpes</b>

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.730
<b>Warm Pork Soup
200 Yen</b>

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:11.070
<b>Café</b>

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:13.280
<b>Closed</b>

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:15.370
Okay, people, it's time for the culture festival!

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.570
Hey, now... What's with those faces?

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:20.920
Sell enough today and there's 
a prize in it for you!

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:24.540
The café or food stand that sells the most

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:27.750
<b>Café & Food Stand Gross Sales</b>

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.180
gets extra funds for their post-festival party!

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:30.980
Can we go bowling or 
do karaoke for the party?

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.140
Sure, as long as you're not out too late.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:35.590
Really?

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:37.640
Go!

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.560
Let's do this, Sensei!

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.880
Let's see what you can do, Tsukimiya.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.820
<i>Why is he suddenly getting into it?</i>

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:46.020
<i>I've got a bad feeling...</i>

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:05.370
<b>A Destructive God Sits Next to Me</b>

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.700
It's time for the grand opening

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:20.070
<b><i>Delusion 7</i></b>

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:20.830
of the Japanese-style café
 "Purgatory's Teahouse."

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:21.910
<i>Hang on.</i>

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:23.740
<b>Purgatory's Teahouse</b>

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:23.740
<i>Why did you name it that?</i>

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:27.360
Hey, Seri-kun, you haven't changed! 
Customers will be here any minute.

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:29.630
But I'm working in the back...

00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:31.480
You know I'd never allow that.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:34.190
<b><u>Purgatory's Teahouse</u>

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:34.360
<b>Special Kusa Dango 

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:34.360
Now get to it! Come on!

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:37.460
Wh-Why am I the only one who has to wear this?

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:39.390
You look great, Koyukichi-dono!

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:43.180
I wish you'd blow on me while
you blow on that pinwheel!

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:44.510
The hour of judgment is here.

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:45.840
Let's go, Gestöber.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.100
<i>Go without me!</i>

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:48.950
Listen, you two.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:50.740
You want to do a duet with Seri-kun

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:53.580
to make him remember your
past bond, right, Hanadori?

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:58.420
And you want Seri-kun to crack your head open 
with a bowling ball, right, Mogami-kun?

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:00.070
Then there's only one thing to do...

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:03.630
And that's whatever it takes to get 
us to the top of the sales charts!

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:04.540
Yeah!

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:06.600
<i>Why are they all coming together?</i>

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.750
<i>What are they planning? They're scaring me!</i>

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:13.760
<i>I wonder if I can just find a way to ditch
 instead of dealing with this stress...</i>

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:14.710
Are you open?

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:17.380
<i>I want to see Sumiso-san in cat ears!</i>

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.600
Seri-kun, we have a customer!

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:21.180
Welcome!

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:25.510
Here you go. Our special kusa dan—

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:27.840
What?

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.930
<i>H-Hanadori-kun?</i>

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:31.640
<i>You're sweating! Really sweating!</i>

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:34.420
<i>Huh?</i>

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:40.700
My apologies, ladies.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:43.320
I brought you a new plate.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:46.530
I also added a folded lotus flower
napkin as an apology.

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:48.250
<i>Wh-What was that?</i>

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:48.240
Oh, wow!

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:50.080
<i>Where does he get those skills?</i>

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.560
Now let's make some money!

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:56.630
<b><u>Purgatory's Teahouse</u>

00:03:56.630 --> 00:04:00.280
It all sounds delicious, my senpais!

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.460
Oh, Helius!

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:02.680
You came, huh?

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:04.680
Welcome, Hibiki-kun!

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:07.000
I've been waiting for you.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:10.480
I've got a special seat with your name on it.

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:12.560
Welcome!

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.200
Your water and hand towel.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:15.180
Your menu.

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:16.490
Stay as long as you like.

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:17.900
Order whatever you like.

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:22.360
Menu

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:22.920
I can't believe the warm welcome I'm getting!

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:24.900
Um, I'll take whatever you recommend.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:26.580
I recommend everything.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.040
I need one of everything!

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:30.250
Okay!

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:33.420
That will be 140,000 yen, sir.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:34.290
Is that all right?

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:35.960
<i>Of course it's not!</i>

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:37.760
It was a joke. It was just a joke, okay?

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:37.740
<i>How did you come up with that number?</i>

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:39.840
<i>The poor guy froze up.</i>

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:42.170
<i>Don't try to rip off the underclassmen!</i>

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:44.130
Th-Thank you for the food.

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:46.000
I'm sorry. I'm really sorry!

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:46.000
Thank you for coming!

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:50.310
I'm disgusting! I'm a loser!

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:50.310
Hibiki-kun!

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:53.720
If any bad rumors get started, 
we can forget our post-festival party.

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:59.080
Oh, I guess you're pretty
serious about this too, huh?

00:04:59.080 --> 00:04:59.940
<i>No!</i>

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:02.160
Hey, may I come in?

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:03.840
Oh, sorry.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:05.610
I'll show you to your... seat...

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:09.520
Shi-chan, you said this
was a European-style café!

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:11.500
We don't belong here!

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:14.360
I-I'm Takeda...

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:16.720
Takeda Shicharing Shikimune.

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:17.760
We've never met.

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:18.500
<i>Who?!</i>

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:21.370
<i>What even is "Shicharing"? 
It sounds like "featuring"!</i>

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:23.630
<i>I know you. You're the guy 
from Dead Bull, right?</i>

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:24.750
<i>What is this?</i>

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:26.640
<i>Is that supposed to be a disguise?</i>

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:27.230
What are you going to get, Shi-chan?

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:29.420
<i>Did he come to check up on Hanadori again?</i>

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:31.630
<i>It'd be easier if he just acted normal.</i>

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:34.940
Your water and hand towel.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.700
Please enjoy yoursmelves.

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:44.870
<i>Huh?</i>

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:48.490
Whoopsie! I messed up my line!

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:49.710
<i>"Whoopsie," my foot!</i>

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:52.880
<i>I see. He didn't notice.</i>

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:55.290
<i>He's so obsessed with Hanadori-kun, too...</i>

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:56.180
<i>Poor guy.</i>

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:57.810
Miguel...

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:02.720
After all our passionate concerts together, 
you didn't recognize me at all?

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:05.180
Perhaps time has dulled your blade too much.

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:07.880
Uh, isn't that what the disguise was for?

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:14.580
Sir, all of our kusa dango were
handmade by Hanadori.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:14.810
<b><u>Purgatory's Teahouse</u></b>

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:17.690
Be yummy! Be yummy!

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:20.720
Why don't you try one?

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:22.160
I'll take them.

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:24.120
Not one, but all of them.

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:25.080
Wow!

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:29.450
Handled by Miguel! Just like me!

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:32.720
I shall take them all into my body!

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:33.780
Thanks for your patronage!

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:36.520
<i>If you can say something that embarrassing,</i>

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:38.320
<i>then why can't you just say, "It's me"?</i>

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:39.800
Hey, Koyuki!

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:41.350
Workin' hard?

00:06:41.350 --> 00:06:43.400
Yeah. You want something to drink?

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:46.300
No, thanks. This place is full of weirdos.

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:50.260
Anyway, come by my class when you can.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:54.600
Goth Loli Girls
<b>Fortune-Telling</b>

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:54.600
<b>Fortune-Telling</b>

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:54.600
It's the "Poison-Tongued Goth Loli 
Fortune-Telling Café."

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:59.250
So I want Koyukichi-dono to punish me,

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:02.070
but he always refuses with kind words.

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:03.660
What should I do?

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:06.560
<i>What kind of question is that?</i>

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:10.420
You never change, Onii-sama.

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:13.560
Get on the ground and offer to be his chair.

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:15.370
<i>What kind of advice is— "Onii-sama"?!</i>

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.120
<i>Wait, what?</i>

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:20.160
<i>The sister Mogami-kun mentioned 
was his twin, wasn't she?</i>

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:22.340
<i>Huh? Was she like this?</i>

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:24.500
<i>Wait, haven't I seen her somewhere before?</i>

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:33.370
<i>Wait, why would you ask your 
sister something like that?!</i>

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:34.270
Are you my sister?!

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:35.720
<i>Are you blind, Onii-sama?</i>

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:37.280
Koyuki Seri...

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:38.690
I remember him.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:43.140
On the day of the painting competition,

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:47.880
I sketched him sobbing after he didn't
make it to the bathroom in time.

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:51.180
<i>Stop torturing me the same 
way your brother does!</i>

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:54.620
So, what do you all want?

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:56.680
U-Uh... What was it again?

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:59.180
We can't have you stealing
the number one spot,

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:00.710
so we came to wreck your dojo!

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:02.880
This is a fortune-telling café.

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:06.140
Yes, which is why I'm going to 
fight you with fortune-telling.

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:07.170
<i>What is he talking about?</i>

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:08.430
I can do it, too.

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:09.630
I don't even need tools.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:12.060
I listen to the voice of the universe.

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:15.500
Everything is occurring as 
destiny has foreordained.

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:17.940
I simply watch.

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:20.670
What you're doing isn't real fortune-telling.

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:25.140
It's a combination of knowledge and wisdom 
gained through obsessive observation.

00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:27.800
And the cards are just props.

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:30.480
Am I wrong, Mogami Suzuran-san?

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:32.700
So?

00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:36.190
Are you telling me to close up shop
if I don't want you telling everyone?

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:36.900
Nope.

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:39.740
Just come by our café and buy something.

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:43.600
<i>Wh-What are you up to, Tsukimiya-kun?</i>

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:46.370
You're going to poison the tea.

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:48.900
I read the fortunes of everyone in that class,

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:52.420
and yours said, "Stay away 
from Tsukimiya Utsugi."

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:53.450
<i>It was right!</i>

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:58.020
But your coming has been foreordained.

00:08:58.020 --> 00:08:59.930
I can tell by looking in your eyes.

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:07.300
Eyes...

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:10.280
Yes. Look into my eyes.

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:16.350
Good girl...

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:21.680
Mogami-san!

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:22.890
What happened, my sister?!

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:24.630
Wh-Wh-What did you do, Tsukimiya-kun?!

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:26.880
She just passed out a little.

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.970
What did you do, though?! And wait...

00:09:28.970 --> 00:09:31.610
You opened your eyes!

00:09:30.370 --> 00:09:32.000
Shh, Seri-kun!

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:33.670
People will catch on to my plan.

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:37.300
<b>A
w
a
r
d</b>

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:39.350
We're number one!

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:41.220
You did it, guys!

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:44.510
<i>After that, Mogami-san just got up,</i>

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:43.130
For real?

00:09:43.130 --> 00:09:44.290
I can't believe it.

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:45.580
That's kinda amazing!

00:09:44.510 --> 00:09:47.690
<i>came to our café, and then didn't leave.</i>

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:48.730
<i>What </i>was<i> that?</i>

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:51.440
A peaceful way for us to win!

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:53.860
<i>Was it some kind of mind control?</i>

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:55.360
<i>Isn't that going too far?</i>

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:56.840
You've got it all wrong.

00:09:58.690 --> 00:10:00.590
She acted of her own free will.

00:10:00.590 --> 00:10:02.620
It was simply foreordained.

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:05.560
It was the will of the universe.

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:19.420
Hooray! Hooray! Hooray!

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:07.120
<i>Sounds like bullshit.</i>

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:09.410
<i>He really will do whatever it takes.</i>

00:10:09.410 --> 00:10:11.130
<i>I hope I never make an enemy of him...</i>

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:13.590
What's wrong, Gestöber?

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:16.670
We won, but you still look so down.

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:19.440
<i>I guess it's fine.</i>

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:23.460
<i>But in the end, I never did get 
to see Sumiso-san in cat ears.</i>

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:24.510
<i>I'm just tired.</i>

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:27.200
I see.

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:29.350
You really worked hard, Gestöber.

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:31.040
Good work.

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:32.700
Good boy.

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:38.880
Gestöber.

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:42.170
Don't copy Utsugi-sama!

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:42.160
<i>What are you doing?!</i>

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:44.130
What's the meaning of this, Suzuran?

00:10:44.670 --> 00:10:45.860
Utsugi-sama...

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:46.950
Huh?

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:50.080
The hypnosis should've worn off by now.

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:52.040
<i>Hey! So it really was hypnosis?!</i>

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:57.000
I saw the universe in your eyes.

00:10:57.280 --> 00:10:59.190
It was endlessly vast and deep.

00:10:59.190 --> 00:11:00.970
Everything was there.

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:04.160
Even the darkness of my heart
 was turned toward good.

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:05.970
That's rare.

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:09.350
My sister doesn't like anyone,
but she's sure taken to you.

00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:11.270
Oh, I didn't see you there, Onii-sama.

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:13.440
Tsukimiya-dono,

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:15.960
you may call me your 
older brother if you wish.

00:11:17.390 --> 00:11:19.650
<i>For once, Tsukimiya-kun
doesn't know what to do.</i>

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:21.920
<i>I hope this teaches you a lesson!</i>

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:24.640
<i>...is what I couldn't help thinking.</i>

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:28.830
Look! Here's yours, Gestöber!

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:29.860
<i>I'm not going!</i>

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:33.630
Gestöber!

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:34.650
Let me go!

00:11:33.990 --> 00:11:35.840
<i>Today's the post-festival party.</i>

00:11:34.070 --> 00:11:35.320
Get back here!

00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:39.300
Gestöber, this candy will soothe your throat.

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:41.080
Make sure you're ready for this.

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:43.140
<i>Why is he taking this so seriously?</i>

00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:45.470
I'm so excited!

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:49.970
My duet with Gestöber will heal some
of the darkness in Miguel's heart!

00:11:49.970 --> 00:11:53.300
I'll have him crack my head open
with my own personal bowling ball!

00:11:53.300 --> 00:11:55.300
<i>You guys sure are well-prepared!</i>

00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:58.420
<i>If you want to sing, go sing with Dead Bull.</i>

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:00.260
<i>Weirdo.</i>

00:12:02.190 --> 00:12:03.500
<i>It's a little late to be asking,</i>

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:06.700
<i>but why is Hanadori-kun so obsessed with me?</i>

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:09.570
Come now, Seri-kun-sensei.

00:12:09.570 --> 00:12:11.500
Your protégés are waiting.

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:12.720
<i>I'm not going.</i>

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:17.420
What? If you came, I was going to give you
 a video of Sumiso-san with cat ears.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:18.590
Fine, I'll go!

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:21.300
<b>House of Coffins</b>

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:22.670
<i>So I ended up coming, but...</i>

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:27.210
<i>Why is Mogami's sister here?</i>

00:12:27.900 --> 00:12:30.600
Prettying yourself up
and pretending to be happy

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:36.540
to get back at your ex is like announcing
to the world that you're miserable.

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:39.990
If you really were happy,
there'd be no need to show him that.

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:42.560
Just so we're clear, this isn't fortune-telling.

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:44.760
It's just what my eyes are telling me.

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:46.490
Any time you're putting on an act,

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:48.980
it's because things aren't that way in reality.

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:52.310
Am I right, Koyuki Seri and his merry band?

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:55.120
<i>Please don't act like I'm 
the poster child example.</i>

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:57.100
<i>And what kind of act are you guys putting on?!</i>

00:12:57.100 --> 00:12:58.540
Where is Utsugi-sama?

00:12:59.270 --> 00:13:01.670
Tsukimiya-kun should be around...

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:02.550
Huh?

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:04.090
<i>He was just here.</i>

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:07.450
I was told that when I wish 
to speak with Utsugi-sama,

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:09.910
I need to go through you.

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:11.760
<i>What? Nobody told me that!</i>

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:11.760
Don't screw it up, flunky.

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:15.840
<i>Do your best to take care of everyone,
Seri-kun-sensei!</i>

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:16.940
<b>Tsukimiya Utsugi</b>

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:16.940
I'll send you that
 cat ears video later!

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:17.280
<i>You bastard...</i>

00:13:17.280 --> 00:13:22.230
I'd like to discuss the mysteries of life
 and the universe with Utsugi-sama,

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:24.180
but he always hides himself away.

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:29.120
So help me find him, Koyuki Seri.

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:31.820
<i>It's really not my problem...</i>

00:13:31.820 --> 00:13:32.760
Hey!

00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:35.670
Gestöber's going to do a duet with me!

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:36.290
<i>Nope.</i>

00:13:37.530 --> 00:13:39.260
Whose turn is it?

00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:42.840
This is for my partner, Gestöber!

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:44.080
"Friends Forever"!

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:47.930
<b>Lyrics</b>

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:47.930
<b>Comp.</b>

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:47.930
<b>~FRIENDS FOREVER~</b>

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:48.880
<i>That's a real song?! Please stop!</i>

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:51.800
Gestöber? You sing, too!

00:13:51.800 --> 00:13:52.720
<i>Please stop...</i>

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:53.940
Sing!

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:56.520
Gestöber, will you sing? Here.

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:56.600
<b>Comrades 
\hComrades</b>

00:13:58.160 --> 00:14:00.520
I'm sorry, but I'm in a hurry.

00:14:02.590 --> 00:14:05.710
Koyuki Seri is coming with
me to look for Utsugi-sama.

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:06.520
Goodbye.

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:08.150
Huh? W-W-Wait!

00:14:08.150 --> 00:14:09.490
Why does everybody grab me by the belt?

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:15.210
I-I'm sorry, Koyukichi-dono!

00:14:15.210 --> 00:14:17.000
My sister's being so selfish.

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.500
Only because you're
worthless as shit, Onii-sama.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.130
<i>That's really mean.</i>

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:26.480
Koyukichi-dono, feel free 
to insult me as she does.

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:28.220
<i>What are you happy about, Onii-sama?</i>

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:30.660
Where did you go, Utsugi-sama?

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:31.950
You must be in the building...

00:14:31.950 --> 00:14:33.440
G-Gestöber!

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:35.140
<i>Hanadori-ku—</i>

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:36.850
K-Karaoke?

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:37.620
<i>Huh?</i>

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:40.860
He's bad at dealing with girls,
but he still tries his best.

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:43.060
You don't seem to have
 realized it, so I'll explain.

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:47.190
Hanadori Kabuto,
Koyuki Seri doesn't like you.

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:48.570
He thinks you're an idiot.

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:50.540
And he's sick of you.

00:14:50.540 --> 00:14:54.010
I don't know what that act 
of yours is supposed to be,

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:56.260
but if you're not willing to 
commit to it, then give it up.

00:14:56.260 --> 00:14:58.800
Knowing all this, if you still 
wish to hang out with him,

00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:01.400
then you should reconsider how you act.

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:03.740
W-Wait, Mogami-san!

00:15:06.430 --> 00:15:08.380
You didn't have to come 
out and say it like that!

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:10.350
You know it was bothering you, though.

00:15:10.350 --> 00:15:11.970
Yet you spoil him anyway.

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:13.670
Are you just pretending to be a good person?

00:15:13.670 --> 00:15:16.510
Or does it not actually bother you that much...

00:15:16.510 --> 00:15:18.340
being "Gestöber"?

00:15:18.340 --> 00:15:20.380
That's not it at all, but...

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:23.670
Go search all the men's restrooms 
in the building, please.

00:15:23.670 --> 00:15:24.610
It's impossible!

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:28.290
If he's seriously trying to hide, 
we'll never find him.

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:31.810
Oh? You've submitted to him
quite a bit, haven't you?

00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:34.390
What about you?

00:15:34.390 --> 00:15:37.100
You said you were going to 
ignore him, but you aren't.

00:15:37.690 --> 00:15:38.700
Indeed.

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:41.700
More than anything, I hated 
men like him who sit back

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:43.630
and laugh at everyone else from above.

00:15:44.090 --> 00:15:46.920
But looking into his eyes, I understood.

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:49.640
There is no above or below, nor good or evil.

00:15:49.640 --> 00:15:51.500
There is, however, everything.

00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:54.120
The heart of the universe
that engulfs everything.

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:57.480
Within its hands, which forgave my foolishness,

00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:59.910
I am but a plaything.

00:16:02.090 --> 00:16:05.900
Most people make that face when I talk.

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:08.580
That face that says,

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:11.610
"I'm the only normal person in this freak show."

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:13.590
If you really are the sane one,

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:17.100
then it's better for them if you make
yourself clear and push them away

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:18.780
rather than playing the victim.

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:23.580
The one people have mistaken for 
a good guy, Koyuki Seri, is you.

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:25.420
<i>Wh-What?!</i>

00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:27.140
You're bothering me.

00:16:25.690 --> 00:16:27.460
<i>But... But...</i>

00:16:27.140 --> 00:16:28.500
Never talk to me again.

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:30.070
<i>When I tell him he's bothering me, 
he just swoons!</i>

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:30.710
<b>Tremble</b>

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:30.710
<b>Tremble</b>

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:30.710
<b>Tremble</b>

00:16:30.070 --> 00:16:31.900
<i>But then sometimes he cries!</i>

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:32.500
<i>This stupid thing!</i>

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:35.760
<i>I mean, yeah, maybe I'm trying to 
come across as the good guy, but...</i>

00:16:36.150 --> 00:16:38.600
<i>Gestöber!</i>

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:39.100
<i>Fine!</i>

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:42.150
<i>You're bothering me,</i>

00:16:42.150 --> 00:16:44.030
<i>so I'm not staying here with you anymore.</i>

00:16:50.510 --> 00:16:53.990
K-Koyukichi-dono, I apologize again.

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:57.800
My sister is a bit of a nasty girl,
sure, but it's all my fault.

00:16:57.800 --> 00:16:59.560
Please scold me!

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:01.450
No, I'm fine.

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:04.700
<i>What Mogami-san says is probably right.</i>

00:17:05.340 --> 00:17:07.870
But... I wonder why...

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:09.120
You're wondering about Suzuran?

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:11.060
No, about Hanadori-kun.

00:17:11.580 --> 00:17:14.260
Why me, I mean.

00:17:14.870 --> 00:17:20.000
At first, I guess he thought
I wanted a friend like him.

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:23.410
Then Tsukimiya-kun said 
something about our past lives.

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:28.560
<i>Gestöber! Gestöber!</i>

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:29.150
But is that really enough to explain
 why he likes me so much?

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:32.480
It shouldn't need to be me.

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:36.000
There must be other people he could 
get along with better, you know?

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:39.710
Not that it really matters, though, right?

00:17:39.710 --> 00:17:44.280
I think I somewhat understand how he feels.

00:17:46.020 --> 00:17:48.120
Oh, you're back, Seri-kun!

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:50.340
See you later, Utsugi-chan!

00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:50.330
Ts-Tsukimiya-kun!

00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:51.700
What were you doing in there?

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:53.330
Forget that, Seri-kun.

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:56.050
Hanadori left already.

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:58.510
<b>House of Coffins</b>

00:18:03.800 --> 00:18:06.560
<i>Wait, wait, wait! Where am I going?</i>

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:08.770
<i>If I go after him now,
 it'll end up like last time...</i>

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:09.600
<i>That's right!</i>

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:11.740
<i>It'll be like every other time
I got worried for nothing!</i>

00:18:11.740 --> 00:18:13.040
What's wrong, Gestöber?

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:15.800
Did you want to walk Cerberus with me?

00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:18.430
<i>I'll want to hit him, 
'cause I'm sure that's what he'll say!</i>

00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:19.240
<i>But...</i>

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:21.000
And he's sick of you.

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:23.790
<i>I did feel that way...</i>

00:18:24.840 --> 00:18:27.340
<i>But I didn't want to say it.</i>

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:30.110
<i>Maybe I was wrong.</i>

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:34.330
<i>When did I get all the way out here?</i>

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:35.420
<i>What am I doing?</i>

00:18:38.250 --> 00:18:40.680
C'mon, cut that out!

00:18:39.570 --> 00:18:40.680
<i>There he is!</i>

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:43.380
<i>He really was playing with Cerberus!</i>

00:18:43.800 --> 00:18:44.940
<i>I'll just go home.</i>

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:47.520
<i>What a waste of a day.</i>

00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:50.100
Hey, Cerberus, would you hear me out?

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:53.320
It wasn't me who saved you the first time.

00:18:53.720 --> 00:18:55.480
It was Gestöber.

00:18:57.250 --> 00:18:59.860
It was on a drizzly morning...

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:13.820
I don't think I can take care of you,
so I'm not going to look at you.

00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:15.100
I'll feel sorry for you if I do.

00:19:15.100 --> 00:19:17.780
<i>The cool-headed Koyuki-kun told a lie! Wow!</i>

00:19:17.780 --> 00:19:18.960
<i>That's so cliché!</i>

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:20.570
<i>Wait, did that happen?</i>

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:22.390
<i>Maybe it did...</i>

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:23.930
<i>Was that Cerberus?</i>

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:26.680
<i>Also, don't make up my dialogue.</i>

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:28.390
<i>I definitely didn't say it that way!</i>

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:30.930
He's so nice, that Gestöber!

00:19:30.930 --> 00:19:32.620
And you know what else?

00:19:32.620 --> 00:19:34.980
When we were deciding on the class rep...

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:37.550
Fine. I guess someone's gotta do it.

00:19:37.550 --> 00:19:38.790
You're so cool!

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:39.440
<i>I did </i>not<i> say that!</i>

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:43.460
<i>I'm starting to worry about
how Hanadori-kun sees me.</i>

00:19:40.050 --> 00:19:43.200
Good boy! Good boy!

00:19:43.460 --> 00:19:44.740
So, you see,

00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:48.910
I was really happy to get back
my old relationship with him.

00:19:49.440 --> 00:19:52.280
Although he may actually hate me.

00:19:52.280 --> 00:19:54.880
Maybe we aren't friends forever.

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:56.020
<i>That's right.</i>

00:19:56.020 --> 00:19:57.930
<i>It's all just a fantasy.</i>

00:19:58.350 --> 00:20:01.760
<i>It's better if you make yourself 
clear and push them away.</i>

00:20:03.820 --> 00:20:04.910
Hanadori-kun.

00:20:05.820 --> 00:20:07.470
G-Gestöber?

00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:10.580
I know I've said this plenty of times,

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:14.760
but my name isn't Gestöber.

00:20:14.760 --> 00:20:15.730
It's Koyuki Seri.

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:19.260
I don't fight anything,
and we're not comrades in arms.

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:20.500
Gestöb—

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:20.500
But...

00:20:21.980 --> 00:20:23.910
If you'll just call me by my name,

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:27.260
I think we can be normal
classmates together... probably.

00:20:29.990 --> 00:20:31.460
Thanks for the candy.

00:20:34.180 --> 00:20:36.760
Oh, and we're going bowling now.

00:20:36.760 --> 00:20:39.550
If you leave, we won't have
enough people to form teams.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:41.340
Okay, got it.

00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:44.040
U-Um, thank you, Gest—

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:47.270
No, um... I mean... K-K-Ko...

00:20:47.270 --> 00:20:49.470
Koyuki!

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:54.940
<b><i>SMASH!</i></b>

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:56.330
That's creepy! Just call me Gestöber!

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:04.320
Why are you both soaked?

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:07.620
<i>What am I doing?!</i>

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:09.890
<i>Nothing's changed at all!</i>

00:21:09.890 --> 00:21:12.080
Koyuki Seri is a failure of a man,

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:12.680
RIP
Koyuki

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:12.680
RIP
Koyuki

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:12.680
RIP
Koyuki

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:12.680
RIP
Koyuki

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:14.540
more influenced by his
emotions than I thought.

00:21:12.680 --> 00:21:14.540
RIP Koyuki

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:17.750
<b>Current Turn: Koyuki</b>

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:17.750
That's part of what makes him special.

00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:19.810
Gestöber said I can call him Gestöber!

00:21:17.770 --> 00:21:20.120
And Hanadori Kabuto...

00:21:19.810 --> 00:21:21.960
And that he'll never leave my side!

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:23.720
He pushes, pushes, pushes, pushes,
 and then suddenly pulls.

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:23.720
Did he? That's nice.

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:26.940
He seems to assume by default
that others love him.

00:21:25.020 --> 00:21:27.910
Maybe I'll try calling him Koyuki again!

00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:29.340
He's more impish than I thought...

00:21:29.340 --> 00:21:30.680
and more of a puppy.

00:21:30.940 --> 00:21:34.600
It's more like Seri-kun is just
too much of a pushover.

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:36.410
I'm so happy!

00:21:36.410 --> 00:21:39.980
He'll dance for me now without
me having to intervene at all.

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:43.820
Miguel is an angel... and a little devil.

00:23:15.060 --> 00:23:15.970
Here's the video 
I promised to send you.

00:23:15.190 --> 00:23:17.580
<i>Thus the culture festival came to an end,</i>

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:20.740
<i>and I calmed my soul by watching 
Sumiso-san dance in cat ears...</i>

00:23:20.740 --> 00:23:24.960
Which one is Sumiso-san?
Those aren't the right cat ears!

00:23:25.500 --> 00:23:28.120
H-How did Menukoroirya
become a moe character?

00:23:28.120 --> 00:23:30.520
You made Tsukimiya-kun the 
chief animation director.

00:23:30.520 --> 00:23:32.980
Damn! Her bo— They're shaking!

00:23:32.980 --> 00:23:35.940
I just wanted Menukoroirya's butt to shake!

00:23:35.940 --> 00:23:39.270
I'll have to add a chief
animation director supervisor!
